From 6446cce14c8c6574a42975134ec54f8a07dc8e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rl-infra <rl-infra@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:04:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(token-capture): an empty reply is not a terminal call

A harness that drops a reply with no visible text and no tool call (Claude
Code after a max_tokens reply) and re-sends the request leaves the dropped
call as a childless sibling of the continuation. Terminal selection then
finds two leaves and rejects the rollout as ambiguous_terminal.

Record empty_reply on the CallRecord (from the normalized response items,
so reasoning-only and empty-text replies count) and make terminal selection
prefer a non-empty sibling when no candidate has children. Two non-empty
siblings remain ambiguous, as before.
